  "all_fixed_order_inference_chain": [
    {
      "argument": "The arbitrary-m affine chain rule applies to both actual xi/v columns. The wave constructor literally reuses sign.values and sign.derivativeMaps and adds only theta's identity column. Higher coordinate derivatives vanish on fixed-label charts. A derivative of length m costs at most (32404*S_ref)^m and preserves the epsilon exponent.",
      "evidence": "common_y:39-63,71-109; global_angular_code:73-117",
      "id": "T1",
      "requires": [
        "P_PRIMARY",
        "P_SUPPORT",
        "P_DOMAIN"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argument": "For K=Q_ref/Q_label, s_label(P)=K*s_ref because 2D+2h=1 and the actual monotone root is unique on the active overlap. X, eta and Q*s are invariant. All actual background profile/cutoff bodies therefore coincide, with velocity scaling K^A (radial b uses epsilon_ref=K^h*epsilon_label) and pressure K^(2A). Whole Y-dependent mean correction keeps the identity Y map and inverse slow chart; no inverse torus cover or replacement mean is assumed.",
      "evidence": "global_band_code:70-97; initialized_angular_code:113-122,128-159",
      "id": "T2",
      "requires": [
        "P_MEAN",
        "P_DOMAIN"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argument": "The native result is an exact function identity, not equality at finitely many points. Separate all-order source bounds supply smoothness. Differentiating equal smooth functions gives every fixed coefficient derivative identity without a fresh native jet run. Dr squared retains derivatives of the R-dependent fast coefficient. Mean-pressure terms cancel linearly before the wave estimate.",
      "evidence": "angular_producer_code:205-210; radial_axial_producer_code:251-255",
      "id": "T3",
      "requires": [
        "P_PRIMARY",
        "P_MEAN",
        "P_NATIVE",
        "T1",
        "T2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argument": "The actual homogeneous principal equation leaves +psi_prime*t. The regular coefficient contains every principal-on-curl, slow, phase, pressure, viscous, frame, mean-wave and same-label square term. Exact full-curl divergence removes the longitudinal k loss, without assuming n dot a=0 for the full amplitude. Finite Leibniz rules at any fixed m preserve alpha=1-3*kappa_s for modes +/-1 and alpha=1-kappa_s for +/-2. Frozen ratio factors are bounded by 16*4^(m+L); no extra epsilon loss is introduced. Thus actual G_wave belongs to W_(99997/100000), hence W_(7/10).",
      "evidence": "written_all_order_proof:13-58; wave_consumer:146-248",
      "id": "T4",
      "requires": [
        "P_PRIMARY",
        "P_MEAN",
        "T1",
        "T2",
        "T3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argument": "The actual cutoff tail retains +psi_prime*t. Its source Gaussian/length nodes give c>0 and exp(-c*S_label). Each fixed physical derivative, including chart, normalization and carrier factors, is bounded by a finite C*Q^(-M)*S_label^P*exp(-c*S_label). With Q=2^(-ell), S_label=ell^2 and q>=Q/2 on active-label support, square completion gives C_N=C*2^N*(2P/c)^P*exp((M+N)^2/(2c)) for every N; the P=0 factor is1. Hence F_pulse is flat. No numerical C or new threshold is required.",
      "evidence": "written_all_order_proof:60-77; wave_consumer:250-267; global_angular_code:130-156",
      "id": "T5",
      "requires": [
        "P_PRIMARY",
        "P_SUPPORT",
        "P_DOMAIN",
        "T1",
        "T2",
        "T3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argument": "Original all-order flat joins extend the chart result across guards/relabeling. Finite assembly keeps all three components, all162 source rows, both mean-wave orders and same-row squares. Therefore Pi_nonzero R=G_wave+F_pulse on the original domain. This closes the transport implication only; it does not accept the whole N6-01 tuple or any later N6-02 substep.",
      "evidence": "common_y:108; global_angular_code:166-176; written_all_order_proof:42-48",
      "id": "T6",
      "requires": [
        "P_SUPPORT",
        "T4",
        "T5"
      ]
    }
  ],
